meta {
  name: NewProductVersion
  type: graphql
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/graphql-api
  body: graphql
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  x-xtm-hub-token: {{xtm-hub-token}}
}

body:graphql {
  mutation NewProductVersion($product: PlatformIdentifier!, $version: String!, $releasedAt: Date) {
    newProductVersion(product: $product, version: $version, releasedAt: $releasedAt) {
      success
    }
  }
}

body:graphql:vars {
  {
    "product": "opencti",
    "version": "6.260409.0",
    "releasedAt": "2026-04-09T10:15:30Z"
  }
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  Ensure xtm-hub-token is defined in environment (requires GENERATE_MANIFEST capability)
  
  Fill variables:
  product: PlatformIdentifier enum value (e.g. opencti, openaev)
  version: product version, e.g. 6.4.0, or an LTS version, e.g. 7.260309.0-lts.8
  releasedAt (optional): publication date of the release, the published_at of the GitHub release, e.g.
  2026-04-09T10:15:30Z. ISO 8601 date-time with an explicit Z or +hh:mm offset, fractional seconds allowed. Used as the
  creation date of the news feed item. Absent or null: the time of the call.
  
  Behaviour:
  - Any invalid version is rejected (INVALID_PLATFORM_VERSION), LTS or not. The LTS suffix must be lowercase (-lts.N).
  - A releasedAt more than 5 minutes ahead of the Hub's clock, not a string, or not an ISO 8601 date-time with a time
    zone is rejected (INVALID_RELEASE_DATE), for every product and version. Nothing is done: no manifest generation,
    no registration, no news feed item. A date up to 5 minutes ahead is accepted and stored as given.
  - For opencti, a non-LTS version requests the connector manifest generation and registers the version. An LTS
    version (-lts.N suffix) skips both.
  - For openaev, never a manifest generation nor a registration, whatever the version. Example: product openaev,
    version 3.261104.0 only creates the news feed item below.
  - For opencti and openaev, every valid version also creates one GITHUB_RELEASE news feed item, once per product
    and version (a later call with the same version does nothing, even once the item is deleted), provisioned to
    the active platforms of that product on the same release track (LTS or not) whose version passes the gate of
    that track. It redirects to the release tag of the GitHub repository of the product. This step runs in the
    background and never fails the mutation. Its creation date is releasedAt, or the time of the call when absent.
    A later call for an existing version ignores releasedAt: the date of the existing item is not updated.
}
